# ai.wing — Change Log & Revert Guide

Running record of every AI-made change to this project. Newest entry at the top.
Each entry lists what changed, why, and how to undo it.

---

## [0006] 2026-09-16 — Re-audit, entity rename, hero photo unmasked

### Re-audit of fidiumfiber.com — one service line was missed

| Line | Offered? | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| Fiber internet | **Yes** | 5 speed tiers |
| **Home phone** | **Yes** | Nav item at `/home-phone`. 20+ calling features. **No published price.** |
| Cable | No | Only appears as a comparison ("40x faster than cable upload speeds") |
| TV | No | Zero product usage; all matches were CSS class names |
| Mobile | No | Zero product usage; all matches were CSS class names |
| Bundles | No | Zero matches anywhere |

**Home phone has been added** as a `serviceLine: 'phone'` plan. Fidium publishes
no rate for it, so the plan carries no `price` — the lockup and its CTA switch
themselves to **"Call for pricing"**, exactly as the architecture intended. It
renders last, per the canonical service-line order.

`FinePrint` now reads `plansFor('fiber')` rather than all `PLANS`, so the specs
table stays a fiber speed comparison and does not gain a phone column.
`PlanCard` falls back to the plan name when a plan has no speed.

### Hero photograph unmasked

The white scrim is gone entirely — the photograph renders at full strength.
Legibility is handled on the **text** side instead, so nothing covers the image:

| Element | Change | Measured against this photo |
|---|---|---|
| Headline | unchanged (ink) | **10.1:1** — passes AA |
| Sub-copy | slate-600 → slate-700, medium weight | 4.8:1 → **6.5:1** |
| Eyebrow | translucent pill → **solid white** pill | 2.1:1 (failed) → **4.8:1** |
| "or" divider | slate-400 → slate-600 on a white pill | was failing |
| ZIP helper | slate-500 → slate-700 semibold | was marginal |

Contrast was measured per text band against the actual cropped region of
`hero-home.jpg`, not estimated.

### Why-fiber section is now the photograph

`family-connected.jpg` is the full section background rather than an inset band.
The section flips to dark: white heading, translucent `bg-ink/55` glass cards,
lime icon chips. A **dark** scrim (`bg-ink/72` plus a vertical gradient) sits
over it — that photo is a dim evening room, so light text needs it. The section
wipe in `app/page.tsx` changed from `from="slate"` to `from="ink"` to match.

### Navbar button

The wide green glow (`0 10px 30px -10px rgba(0,174,66,.65)`) is replaced with a
tight two-stop shadow, and the **magnetic hover was removed** — a button that
drifts under the cursor reads as unstable in fixed chrome. Padding tightened to
`px-5 py-2.5`. Applies to the compact mobile icon button too.

### Copy

- "Choose the plan that fits your household" → **"Compare speeds and pricing"**
- "Engineered for consistent performance" → **"The advantages of a fiber-optic connection"**

### Entity rename and copyright

- `SITE.entity` and `SITE.shortName`: `Fiberline Communications LLC` → **`FidiumFiber`**.
  Propagates to all 11 legal pages, the footer, and the structured data.
- The footer copyright line and its `FOOTER.copyright` getter are removed.

Verified: **0** occurrences of "Fiberline" and **0** copyright lines across all
built routes; 95 `tel:` links, all carrying `data-call-cta`.

> ⚠️ **Open compliance issue.** Naming the operating entity "FidiumFiber" makes
> the legal pages self-contradictory — they now read *"FidiumFiber is an
> independent authorized retailer of Fidium Fiber… It is not operated by Fidium
> or its parent company."* Using the carrier's mark as your own business name
> also cuts against the trademark notice on `/trademarks` and against Google
> Ads' affiliate/misrepresentation rules. The display branding can stay as it
> is; what needs to change is `SITE.entity`, which should be the real registered
> company that signs the legal pages. One edit in `lib/content.ts` fixes it.

### To revert this entry

In `lib/content.ts`: restore `entity`/`shortName`, the `copyright` getter, the
two headings, and delete the `phone-home` plan. In `Hero.tsx`: restore the
`from-white/88 via-white/45 to-white/92` scrim and the original text colours.
In `Features.tsx`: restore the light section with the inset lifestyle band. In
`Header.tsx`: restore `magnetic` and the default shadow. In `FinePrint.tsx`:
import `PLANS` again instead of `plansFor('fiber')`.

