## [0003] 2026-09-16 — Copy professionalised, animations trimmed, table bug fixed

### Bug fixed: the fine-print section rendered blank on desktop

The comparison table was wrapped in a `.wipe-in` clip-path reveal. The CSS that
opened the clip was:

```css
.anim [data-reveal='is-in'].wipe-in,   /* same element */
.anim .is-in .wipe-in { … }            /* needs a literal .is-in class */
```

but in the markup `.wipe-in` sat on a **child** of the `[data-reveal]` element,
so neither selector ever matched. The clip stayed at
`inset(0 0 100%)` — the table was clipped to zero height and the section looked
empty between its heading and its footnote.

**Fix:** removed the `.wipe-in` class from `FinePrint.tsx` and deleted the dead
`.wipe-in` CSS block (plus its reduced-motion entry). The table still animates in
via the existing `Reveal` fade-and-rise, and clip-path wipes between sections are
unaffected — those come from `SectionWipe`'s separate `.wipe-diagonal`.

### Copy rewritten for a more professional register

All of it lives in `lib/content.ts`.

| Where | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Hero H1 | "Fiber internet that keeps up with your whole house." | "Symmetrical fiber internet for the connected home." |
| Plans heading | "Pick the speed your home actually needs" | "Choose the plan that fits your household" |
| Why-fiber heading | "A connection built to be boring" | "Engineered for consistent performance" |
| Why-fiber body | "Fiber runs light through glass instead of electrical signal through copper. In practice that means steadier speeds…" | "Fiber-optic lines carry data as light through glass rather than electrical signal through copper. The result is stable throughput during peak hours and upload speeds that match download speeds." |
| Fine-print heading | "Everything in one table, nothing buried" | "Complete specifications, side by side" |
| Fine-print eyebrow | "The honest fine print" | "Plan details" |
| How-it-works heading | "Four steps from call to connected" | "From availability check to installation" |
| How-it-works body | "No paperwork marathon and no guesswork about what is available on your street. Here is the whole process." | "Four steps, handled by a representative who confirms what is available at your service address before any order is placed." |

The fine-print **eyebrow** was not on the request list, but leaving "THE HONEST
FINE PRINT" above a newly formal heading left a tonal mismatch, so it moved too.

### Removed

| Item | Detail |
|---|---|
| Hero visual panel | The dark box with the canvas animation and the "Symmetrical by design / Download / Upload" readout. Hero is now a single centred column. |
| `components/sections/FiberField.tsx` | **Deleted.** The canvas "black hole" field had no remaining consumer. |
| Hero phone + hours | The plain-text `(888) 425-0568` and business hours beside the hero CTA. The **"Call to order" button stays** — only the text block went. |
| How-it-works animation | The scroll-scrubbed gateway assembly SVG and its sticky column. Steps are now a static 4-column grid, and the section became a **server component** (no client JS at all). |
| `useScrollProgress` | Removed from `lib/hooks.ts` — the assembly animation was its only caller. |
| Footer "Ready when you are" band | The whole closing CTA block, including its "Compare plans" button. The footer now opens directly on the column grid. |

### Also

- `FEATURES_SECTION` and `HOW_IT_WORKS_SECTION` added to `lib/content.ts`. Those
  two section headings had been hardcoded in JSX; they are now data like every
  other string on the site.
- Unused imports cleaned from `Hero.tsx` and `Footer.tsx`.

### Verification

- Typecheck and build clean; 18 static pages; homepage **99.6 kB** First Load JS
  (down from 101 kB — the canvas and scroll-progress code are gone).
- Fine-print table measured in the browser at **943 × 825 px, 9 rows × 6 columns** —
  previously 0 × 0.
- Hero contains no visible phone number or hours. The only `888` left in its
  markup is inside the CTA's `tel:` href and aria-label, which the link needs.
- Zero horizontal overflow at 320px.
- All `tel:` links still carry `data-call-cta`; the only CTA label outside the
  header and footer is still "Call to order".

### To revert this entry

Restore the copy strings in `lib/content.ts` from the table above, re-add the
`.wipe-in` class and CSS, and restore `FiberField.tsx`, `useScrollProgress`, the
hero visual column, the hero phone block, the how-it-works assembly animation and
the footer CTA band.

