## [0001] 2026-09-16 — Initial build (from scratch)

**Scope:** Complete Fidium Authorized Retailer one-page landing site.
**Stack:** Next.js 14.2.15 (App Router) · TypeScript (strict) · Tailwind CSS 3.4 · Lenis
**Build result:** clean · 11 static routes · homepage First Load JS **101 kB**

### Files created

#### Configuration
| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `package.json` | Deps: `next`, `react`, `react-dom`, `lenis`. Nothing else at runtime. |
| `tsconfig.json` | Strict TS, `@/*` path alias. |
| `next.config.mjs` | Strict mode, compression, console stripped in production. |
| `tailwind.config.ts` | Official Fidium palette, full 0–100 opacity scale, brand easing/keyframes. |
| `postcss.config.mjs` | Tailwind + Autoprefixer. |
| `.claude/launch.json` | Dev/prod preview servers (ports 3112 / 3111). |

#### Data layer — the single source of truth
| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **`lib/content.ts`** | **Every price, speed, fee, promo, disclosure, FAQ and legal string.** Edit this file alone to update the whole site. |
| `lib/hooks.ts` | Custom animation hooks: in-view, scroll progress, parallax, magnetic, tilt, scrolled, reduced-motion. |

#### Components
| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `components/primitives/PriceLockup.tsx` | **The one price renderer on the site.** `$` + dominant integer (2.5–3.5rem) + muted cents + `/mo`. Falls back to "Call for pricing" when a plan has no price. |
| `components/primitives/CallButton.tsx` | Only component that emits a `tel:` sales link. Every instance carries `data-call-cta`. `CallNumberButton` is the header/footer variant that shows the number. |
| `components/primitives/Reveal.tsx` | `Reveal` (entrance) and `RevealText` (word-by-word, optional brand gradient). |
| `components/primitives/Marquee.tsx` | Infinite CSS ticker; screen readers get the list once. |
| `components/primitives/SectionWipe.tsx` | Clip-path wipe between major sections + SVG fiber path draw. |
| `components/providers/LenisProvider.tsx` | Lenis smooth scroll, dynamically imported after hydration. |
| `components/layout/Logo.tsx` | Custom SVG Fidium-styled wordmark. |
| `components/layout/DisclosureBar.tsx` | Persistent, non-dismissable retailer disclosure. |
| `components/layout/Header.tsx` | Sticky header, anchor nav, solid phone-number button, mobile sheet. |
| `components/layout/Footer.tsx` | Dark 4-column footer modelled on bestfiberinternet.us. |
| `components/layout/LegalPage.tsx` | Shared shell for the four legal routes. |
| `components/sections/Hero.tsx` | Hero + ZIP checker + call button + trust chips + trust marquee. |
| `components/sections/FiberField.tsx` | Canvas "black hole" spiral data field. |
| `components/sections/PlanCard.tsx` | 3D tilt plan card. |
| `components/sections/ServiceLineSection.tsx` | Renders service lines in canonical order; omits lines with no plans. |
| `components/sections/Features.tsx` | Staggered benefits grid. |
| `components/sections/FinePrint.tsx` | Comparison table (desktop) + stacked cards (mobile). |
| `components/sections/HowItWorks.tsx` | Scroll-scrubbed gateway assembly animation. |
| `components/sections/Faq.tsx` | Accordion. |

#### App routes
| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `app/layout.tsx` | Metadata, Inter font, JSON-LD (Organization + Product per plan + FAQPage), global chrome, `.anim` bootstrap script. |
| `app/page.tsx` | Canonical section order. |
| `app/globals.css` | Design tokens, button/chip components, all animation CSS, reduced-motion overrides. |
| `app/privacy/`, `app/terms/`, `app/accessibility/`, `app/do-not-sell/` | Legal routes. |
| `app/icon.svg`, `app/sitemap.ts`, `app/robots.ts` | Favicon, sitemap, robots. |

### Page order as built
```
Top disclosure bar  →  Sticky header  →  Hero  →  Fiber plans  →  Why fiber
  →  Honest fine print  →  How it works  →  FAQ  →  Footer
```

### Service-line audit against fidiumfiber.com
| Line | Offered? | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Fiber | Yes | 5 plans rendered |
| Cable | No | Section omitted entirely |
| Bundles | No | Section omitted entirely |
| TV | No | Section omitted entirely |
| Mobile | No | Section omitted entirely |
| Phone / VoIP | No | Section omitted entirely |

Fidium is a fiber-only ISP. Empty service lines resolve to zero plans, so
`ACTIVE_SERVICE_SECTIONS` filters them out and no placeholder is ever rendered.

### Plan data (verified against the official Fidium price-card data)
| Plan | Speed | Price | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Light use | 300 Mbps | $30/mo | BYO router supported |
| Busy homes | 1 Gig | $50/mo | + 1 month free |
| Power users | 2 Gig | $60/mo | **Best value** · + 1 month free |
| Creators & pros | 5 Gig | $80/mo | WiFi 7 · + 1 month free |
| Future ready | 8 Gig | $130/mo | WiFi 7 · + 1 month free |

All symmetrical. Unlimited data, no contracts, free professional installation.

### Brand colors (sampled from the live fidiumfiber.com stylesheet)
`#93D500` lime · `#00AE42` green · `#008533` deep green · `#003595` navy ·
`#F97E19` promo orange · `#0B1220` ink

### Animations implemented
Scroll-scrubbed gateway assembly · Lenis smooth scroll · canvas black-hole fiber
field · word-by-word text reveals · parallax hero · SVG path draw · magnetic
buttons · clip-path section wipes · 3D card tilt · staggered grid entrances ·
infinite marquee.

All are custom-built on IntersectionObserver, rAF and CSS — **no animation
library** — which is why First Load JS stays at 101 kB. Every one of them is
disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`.

### Negative constraints — all honoured
- No support-routing copy anywhere.
- Hero keeps **both** the ZIP checker and a call button.
- Every CTA outside the header/footer reads "Call to order" (or "Call for
  pricing" automatically if a plan has no price).
- No competitor bashing or "ordering channel" phrasing.
- No cable/TV/mobile/bundle/phone sections and no placeholder cards.
- No Broadband Facts label link.
- No "Pricing observed [date]" or any date stamp.
- No "Is this the official Fidium site?" FAQ.

### Fixes applied during verification (all in the delivered build)

| Fix | File | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Gradient headline words | `Reveal.tsx`, `globals.css` | `background-clip: text` on a parent repaints wrongly once a child is transformed, smearing the words together. Each word now carries its own gradient, stretched to the line width and offset per word, so the ramp stays continuous. |
| No-JS safety net | `layout.tsx`, `globals.css` | Entrance animations start at `opacity: 0`. They are now armed only by an `.anim` class that JavaScript sets before first paint, so a failed script can never leave the page blank. |
| Canvas trail maths | `FiberField.tsx` | Trail vectors were computed against the centre instead of the particle's own previous position, drawing long diagonal streaks instead of a spiral. |
| Mobile fine-print rows | `FinePrint.tsx` | A long value (e.g. "WiFi 7 gateway and extenders included") squeezed the row label to zero width. The row now wraps the value onto its own line instead. |
| Header at 320px | `Logo.tsx`, `Header.tsx` | Logo + call + menu overflowed the row by 10px. The logo's "Authorized Retailer" line is hidden below `sm` (`compact` prop) — the disclosure bar above already states it. |
| ZIP success state | `Hero.tsx` | Replaced an inline phone-number link with a proper "Call to order" button, keeping every CTA on-label and improving conversion. |

### Verification performed

- `tsc --noEmit` clean; production build clean.
- **Pricing is genuinely centralised:** temporarily changing one plan's price and
  speed in `lib/content.ts` updated 14 rendered price locations and 22 speed
  locations across hero, cards, table, FAQ and footer, with zero stale values.
  Reverted afterwards.
- `grep` confirms **no** hardcoded price, speed or CTA label exists in any
  `.tsx` file.
- **Zero horizontal overflow at 320px** — `document.scrollWidth` is exactly 320.
- All 24 `tel:` links carry `data-call-cta`.
- Only CTA label outside the header/footer is "Call to order".
- Banned-phrase sweep across all 6 built routes: clean.
- Omitted service lines (cable, bundle, TV, mobile, phone) render nothing at all.

